-- title:
--   Initial forms multiply: Gh^k lies in (X₀,X₁)^{dk}
-- statement:
--   Let $W$ be a commutative ring, let $G$ and $h$ be formal power series in two variables over $W$ (indexed by `Fin 2`), let $d$ and $k$ be natural numbers, and suppose $h$ lies in the $d$-th power of the ideal generated by $X_0$ and $X_1$. Let $a, b \in W$. The conclusion is a conjunction. First, $G \cdot h^k$ lies in the $(dk)$-th power of the ideal $(X_0, X_1)$. Second, the weighted sum of the coefficients of $G \cdot h^k$ along the monomials $X_0^i X_1^{dk-i}$ of total degree $dk$, namely $\sum_{i=0}^{dk} [X_0^i X_1^{dk-i}](G h^k)\, a^i b^{dk-i}$ (the sum being taken over $i$ in `Finset.range (d*k+1)`, with the exponent of $X_1$ written as the truncated subtraction $dk - i$), equals the constant coefficient of $G$ times the $k$-th power of the corresponding degree-$d$ sum for $h$, $\left(\sum_{i=0}^{d} [X_0^i X_1^{d-i}](h)\, a^i b^{d-i}\right)^{k}$. No hypothesis of positivity on $d$ or $k$, and no invertibility hypothesis on $a$, $b$ or the coefficients, is imposed.
--
--   The two assertions express that the substitution $X_0 \mapsto aT$, $X_1 \mapsto bT$ turns membership in $(X_0,X_1)^d$ into divisibility by $T^d$ and that initial forms multiply: the degree-$dk$ directional coefficient of $Gh^k$ is the product of the constant term of $G$ with the $k$-th power of the degree-$d$ directional coefficient of $h$. In particular the sum attached to $Gh^k$ is a unit as soon as $G(0,0)$ and the sum attached to $h$ are; this is the form in which it is used on the Drinfeld local chart, where it supports [`DrinfeldCurve.LocalChart.exists_mem_pow_isUnit_homogeneous_mul_eval_map_eq_mk_of_monic`](thm.html#DrinfeldCurve.LocalChart.exists_mem_pow_isUnit_homogeneous_mul_eval_map_eq_mk_of_monic) and [`DrinfeldCurve.LocalChart.exists_mem_pow_isUnit_homogeneous_mul_mk_pow_eq_mk`](thm.html#DrinfeldCurve.LocalChart.exists_mem_pow_isUnit_homogeneous_mul_mk_pow_eq_mk).
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_MvPowerSeries_mul_pow_mem_span_X_pow_and_sum_coeff_mul_pow_eq_constantCoeff_mul_pow.lean

